{#
  SITE HEADER — Figma 184:13318. Driven by _data/hero.js.

  Replaces the v2 floating bottom nav. That bar was a scroll-spy driven by
  scripts/nav.js; this is plain anchors with no JS at all. nav.js has since been
  deleted in the cleanup sweep, along with the site.nav array that fed it —
  that data is still in _data/site.js and is now unused.

  Hrefs are absolute (/#id) rather than bare fragments so the header behaves
  identically on /work/* and /projects, where those sections don't exist.

  TWO OF THE THREE POINT AT NOTHING RIGHT NOW. /#featured-works and /#contact
  were ids on the old Projects and Footer blocks, both removed in the sweep;
  they come back when Testimonials (187:2301) and Footer (289:2233) are built.
  /#about-me was repointed off the timeline's old #all-about-me at the same
  time and does resolve.

  The rule below the header and the rules either side of the container are
  three separate 1px borders in Figma at two different opacities — see
  _nav.css, where they are the only thing the two --fig-rule-* tokens exist for.
#}

<header class="site-header">
  <div class="site-header__inner">
    <a class="site-header__logo" href="/">
      <img
        class="site-header__mark"
        src="{{ hero.assetPath }}/{{ hero.header.logo.file }}"
        alt=""
        width="{{ hero.header.logo.size }}"
        height="{{ hero.header.logo.size }}"
      />
      <span class="site-header__name"
        ><strong class="site-header__name-lead">{{ hero.header.name.lead }}</strong
        >{{ hero.header.name.rest }}</span
      >
    </a>

    <nav class="site-header__nav" aria-label="Primary">
      <ul class="site-header__links">
        {%- for item in hero.header.links %}
          <li><a class="site-header__link" href="{{ item.href }}">{{ item.label }}</a></li>
        {%- endfor %}
      </ul>
      <a class="site-header__cta" href="{{ hero.header.cta.href }}">{{ hero.header.cta.label }}</a>
    </nav>
  </div>
</header>
